  "verification": "Tilted-cut geometry/frame and fullimagegradientFD2tests passed3.92s. CorrectedHOS tests plus those controls6passed2.79s, including full-auxiliary volume and reciprocal work on resolved modes with padding2/3.",
  "review": "Independent source reviewer approved CG/rotation/clipping, reflected gradients, odd padding/normalization and bodycontinuation; separate reviewer derived formalDNO truncation. True-plane imagegap guards and explicit accelerationpotential normalization were added. Whole-panel/Fouriergraph cutting and dynamics remain unqualified.",
  "conclusions": [
    "Order4 improves bodycontinuation substantially overorder2; order6/8 add little for these particular fields. At128m/513/order4, largerimageclearance case has bodypotential relativeerrors2.47e-5/3.03e-6 and normalerrors9.0e-5/1.82e-5. These are known exterior fields, not an unknown bodyBVP.",
    "Doubling64->128m at~.25m spacing reduces larger-clearance heave-like globalgradienterror.009615->.002401 and nearhull.001206->.000150. Aperiodic referencegraphflux .2976->.1494 while periodicauxiliaryflux remainsroundoff. This exposes finiteperiodic/aperiodic boundary mismatch; do not call the referenceflux a conservationfailure.",
    "Smaller-clearance rotation-like gradienterror stays~.0019 at fixedspacing underdomainenlargement, consistent with a separate resolutionlimit. A domaincontrol doesnot resolve all errors.",
    "The old HOShelper included slope times horizontalorderM without matchingverticalorderM+1. Correcting formalorder preserves volume and reciprocity on resolvedperiodic controls without addedFFTs/meanprojection. AtM4 meanflux1.20e-6->~6e-18; exactreferenceflux error1.03e-4->2.48e-5. AllCartesianvelocities andflatcoefficients unchangedbitwise in the owned comparison.",
    "Thefluxfix doesNOT explain or change the above Cartesiangradient errors. It also doesnot prove fullhull pressure/action consistency, physicalexterior massbalance or Hamiltonian coupling.",
    "These favorable sourceimages all lie above the HOSreferenceplane. Exteriorpoles near a trough canlie below otherfluidtargets; global exponentialcontinuation then has a Rayleigh-type limitation. This remains an open risk, not a new productionrequirement or an established failure of the canonicalcase."
  ],
